===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₃reǵ-}}
{{bor+|en|hi|राजा}} and {{bor|en|ur|راجا|tr=rājā}}, from {{der|en|sa|राजन्||king, prince}}, from {{der|en|inc-pro|*Hrā́ȷ́ā||king}}, from {{der|en|iir-pro|*Hrā́ȷ́ā}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₃rḗǵ-ō}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*h₃rḗǵs|t=ruler, king}}. {{doublet|en|Rex|rex|roy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɑː.d͡ʒə/|/ˈɹɑː.ʒə/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-rajah.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹaː.ha/|a=Philippines}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑːd͡ʒə|ɑːʒə|s=2}}
* {{hyph|en|ra|jah}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[Hindu]] [[prince]] or [[ruler]] in [[India]].
# Any of various [[nymphalid]] butterflies of the [[genus]] {{taxlink|Charaxes|genus}}.

